# Playwright's downloaded browser bundles (Chromium/WebKit). Not ignored, biome
# with vcs.useIgnoreFile scans the whole browser distribution and fails on its
# own bundled helper scripts - and the shared file lister (scripts/source-files.ts)
# hands every gate a browser bundle to walk. Ignored ⇒ invisible, as intended.
.playwright-browsers/
# Scratch audit output. A handful of curated docs under audit/ (AUDIT.md,
# AUDIT_REPORT_BACKUP_IMPORT.md, BUNDLE_OPTIMIZATION.md, WEBMCP.md, …) are
# tracked on purpose even though this rule matches them: the shared file lister
# resolves through `git check-ignore --no-index`, so a tracked-but-ignored file
# is intentionally invisible to every gate - the same reason biome.json's
# useIgnoreFile skips it. Put new scratch reports here, never a curated doc.
audit/
playwright-report.zip
docs/TEST_COVERAGE_PLAN.md
scripts/patch-locale-batch2.ts
scripts/patch-locale-batch3.ts
toggle.png
compare-talis.cjs
